This is honeydoo, an existing, tested Next.js 16 app. Read BOLT_PROMPT.md before any change and follow it on every change.
Never rebuild or restructure. Keep the data layer in src/lib/db.ts (plain SQL, pg with PGlite fallback); never switch to supabase-js or generated data code.
Schema changes: new file in db/migrations, then npm run db:bolt. Never edit old migrations.
Customers never pay a fee; the shop pays $1 per completed order via Square. Totals are computed only on the server. Orders are marked paid only by verified Square webhooks or server read-back.
Secrets stay in environment variables and server code only.
No em dashes and no emojis anywhere (UI, content, code, commits). Minimal, Silicon Valley aesthetic. Do not alter the bee logo.
Run npm run typecheck and npm test after every change.
